f", "x": 5.6000000000000005, "y": -4, "level": 4, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 3, "latex": "\\mathbf{L} = \\mathbf{r} \\times \\mathbf{p} = I \\boldsymbol{\\omega}, \\quad \\boldsymbol{\\tau}_{\\text{net}} = \\frac{d\\mathbf{L}}{dt}", "desc": "Conserved without external torque: skaters spin faster pulling arms in.", "prereqs": ["moment-inertia", "momentum", "torque"], "children": [], "order": 44}, "archimedes": {"name": "Archimedes' principle (buoyancy)", "topic": "Fluids", "color": "#f4845f", "x": -4.800000000000001, "y": -2, "level": 2, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 2, "latex": "F_B = \\rho_{\\text{fluid}} V_{\\text{submerged}} g", "desc": "The upward push equals the weight of the displaced fluid. Float if your average density is lower.", "prereqs": ["density", "weight"], "children": [], "order": 20}, "beats": {"name": "Beats", "topic": "Sound", "color": "#4a6fa5", "x": -0.8, "y": -6, "level": 6, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "f_{\\text{beat}} = |f_1 - f_2|", "desc": "Two close frequencies produce a slow pulsing loudness. Tuners listen for the beats to die out.", "prereqs": ["standing-wave"], "children": [], "order": 49}, "bernoulli": {"name": "Bernoulli's equation", "topic": "Fluids", "color": "#f4845f", "x": -0.8, "y": -4, "level": 4, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 3, "latex": "P_1 + \\tfrac{1}{2}\\rho v_1^2 + \\rho g y_1 = P_2 + \\tfrac{1}{2}\\rho v_2^2 + \\rho g y_2", "desc": "Energy conservation for flowing fluid: fast flow means low pressure. That is how wings lift.", "prereqs": ["continuity", "energy-cons", "pressure-depth"], "children": [], "order": 40}, "carnot": {"name": "Carnot efficiency", "topic": "Thermodynamics", "color": "#e07a5f", "x": 0, "y": -5, "level": 5, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "e_{\\max} = 1 - \\frac{T_C}{T_H} \\quad \\text{(Kelvin)}", "desc": "No heat engine can beat this. Real engines do worse; the gap is friction and irreversibility.", "prereqs": ["first-law"], "children": [], "order": 47}, "centripetal": {"name": "Centripetal acceleration", "topic": "Newton's Laws", "color": "#e07a5f", "x": 4.800000000000001, "y": -1, "level": 1, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 2, "latex": "a_c = \\frac{v^2}{r} \\quad \\text{toward the center}", "desc": "Turning requires inward acceleration. Banked curves and orbits both come from here.", "prereqs": ["newton2", "vel-def"], "children": [], "order": 16}, "cm": {"name": "Center of mass", "topic": "Momentum", "color": "#f2cc8f", "x": -6.4, "y": 0, "level": 0, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 0, "latex": "x_{\\text{cm}} = \\frac{\\sum m_i x_i}{M}", "desc": "The balance point; the system moves as if all mass were there.", "prereqs": [], "children": [], "order": 0}, "continuity": {"name": "Continuity equation", "topic": "Fluids", "color": "#f4845f", "x": -4.800000000000001, "y": 0, "level": 0, "leverage": 1, "n_prereq": 0, "latex": "A_1 v_1 = A_2 v_2 \\quad \\text{(incompressible flow)}", "desc": "Narrow pipe, faster flow. What flows in must flow out.", "prereqs": [], "children": ["bernoulli"], "order": 1}, "decibel": {"name": "Decibel scale", "topic": "Sound", "color": "#4a6fa5", "x": -2.4000000000000004, "y": -4, "level": 4, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "\\beta = 10 \\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{I}{I_0}\\right), \\quad I_0 = 10^{-12} \\, \\text{W/m}^2", "desc": "Logarithmic because ears are. Every 10 dB is a factor of 10 in intensity.", "prereqs": ["intensity"], "children": [], "order": 39}, "density": {"name": "Density", "topic": "Fluids", "color": "#f4845f", "x": -3.2, "y": 0, "level": 0, "leverage": 4, "n_prereq": 0, "latex": "\\rho = \\frac{m}{V}, \\quad \\text{water: } 1000 \\, \\text{kg/m}^3", "desc": "Mass per volume. Ice floats because it is less dense than liquid water.", "prereqs": [], "children": ["archimedes", "pressure-depth"], "order": 2}, "doppler": {"name": "Doppler effect", "topic": "Sound", "color": "#4a6fa5", "x": -6.4, "y": -2, "level": 2, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "f' = f \\frac{v \\pm v_o}{v \\mp v_s} \\quad \\text{(top signs: observer toward source)}", "desc": "Approaching motion squeezes wavelengths and raises pitch. Used in radar and astronomy.", "prereqs": ["wave-speed"], "children": [], "order": 19}, "elastic": {"name": "Elastic collision (1D)", "topic": "Momentum", "color": "#f2cc8f", "x": 0.8, "y": -4, "level": 4, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 2, "latex": "v_{1f} = \\frac{m_1 - m_2}{m_1 + m_2} v_{1i} + \\frac{2 m_2}{m_1 + m_2} v_{2i}", "desc": "Both momentum and kinetic energy conserved. Equal masses: velocities swap.", "prereqs": ["energy-cons", "momentum-cons"], "children": [], "order": 41}, "energy-cons": {"name": "Conservation of mechanical energy", "topic": "Work and Energy", "color": "#81b29a", "x": 1.6, "y": -3, "level": 3, "leverage": 6, "n_prereq": 2, "latex": "K_1 + U_1 = K_2 + U_2 \\quad \\text{(no nonconservative work)}", "desc": "When only conservative forces act, total mechanical energy is fixed.", "prereqs": ["pe-grav", "work-energy"], "children": ["bernoulli", "elastic", "first-law", "shm-energy"], "order": 33}, "entropy": {"name": "Entropy and the second law", "topic": "Thermodynamics", "color": "#e07a5f", "x": 1.6, "y": -5, "level": 5, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "\\Delta S = \\frac{Q_{\\text{rev}}}{T}, \\quad \\Delta S_{\\text{universe}} \\ge 0", "desc": "Disorder never decreases overall. Heat flows hot to cold because that is where the microstates are.", "prereqs": ["first-law"], "children": [], "order": 48}, "first-law": {"name": "First law of thermodynamics", "topic": "Thermodynamics", "color": "#e07a5f", "x": 2.4000000000000004, "y": -4, "level": 4, "leverage": 2, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "\\Delta U = Q - W \\quad \\text{(W = work done BY the system)}", "desc": "Energy conservation with heat counted. Sign conventions vary by textbook; pick one and stay consistent.", "prereqs": ["energy-cons"], "children": ["carnot", "entropy"], "order": 42}, "friction": {"name": "Friction", "topic": "Newton's Laws", "color": "#e07a5f", "x": -6.4, "y": -1, "level": 1, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "f_k = \\mu_k N, \\quad f_s \\le \\mu_s N", "desc": "Kinetic friction is fixed; static friction adjusts up to its maximum to prevent slipping.", "prereqs": ["newton2"], "children": [], "order": 9}, "gravitation": {"name": "Newton's law of gravitation", "topic": "Gravitation", "color": "#e58bb1", "x": -1.6, "y": 0, "level": 0, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 0, "latex": "F = \\frac{G m_1 m_2}{r^2}", "desc": "Inverse-square attraction between any two masses.", "prereqs": [], "children": [], "order": 3}, "ideal-gas": {"name": "Ideal gas law", "topic": "Thermodynamics", "color": "#e07a5f", "x": 1.6, "y": -1, "level": 1, "leverage": 1, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "PV = nRT, \\quad R = 8.314 \\, \\text{J/(mol K)}", "desc": "Pressure, volume, and temperature of an ideal gas in one relation. Use Kelvin.", "prereqs": ["temp-scales"], "children": ["kinetic-theory"], "order": 14}, "impulse": {"name": "Impulse-momentum theorem", "topic": "Momentum", "color": "#f2cc8f", "x": -8, "y": -2, "level": 2, "leverage": 2, "n_prereq": 2, "latex": "\\mathbf{J} = \\Delta \\mathbf{p} = \\int \\mathbf{F} \\, dt", "desc": "A force acting over time changes momentum. Airbags work by stretching dt.", "prereqs": ["momentum", "newton2"], "children": ["momentum-cons"], "order": 18}, "intensity": {"name": "Sound intensity", "topic": "Sound", "color": "#4a6fa5", "x": 0, "y": -3, "level": 3, "leverage": 1, "n_prereq": 2, "latex": "I = \\frac{P}{A}, \\quad I \\propto \\frac{1}{r^2} \\text{ (spherical spreading)}", "desc": "Power per area. Doubling distance quarters the intensity.", "prereqs": ["power", "wave-speed"], "children": ["decibel"], "order": 32}, "ke": {"name": "Kinetic energy", "topic": "Work and Energy", "color": "#81b29a", "x": 0, "y": 0, "level": 0, "leverage": 10, "n_prereq": 0, "latex": "K = \\tfrac{1}{2} m v^2", "desc": "Energy of motion. Quadratic in speed: doubling speed quadruples energy.", "prereqs": [], "children": ["kinetic-theory", "rot-ke", "work-energy"], "order": 4}, "kinematic": {"name": "Constant-acceleration kinematics", "topic": "Kinematics", "color": "#4a6fa5", "x": 6.4, "y": -1, "level": 1, "leverage": 6, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "v = v_0 + at, \\quad x = x_0 + v_0 t + \\tfrac{1}{2} a t^2, \\quad v^2 = v_0^2 + 2a(x - x_0)", "desc": "The three workhorses. Pick the one that skips the variable you don't know.", "prereqs": ["vel-def"], "children": ["projectile", "rot-kin"], "order": 17}, "kinetic-theory": {"name": "Kinetic theory (rms speed)", "topic": "Thermodynamics", "color": "#e07a5f", "x": 4.800000000000001, "y": -2, "level": 2, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 2, "latex": "\\tfrac{1}{2} m \\overline{v^2} = \\tfrac{3}{2} k_B T, \\quad v_{\\text{rms}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{3k_B T}{m}}", "desc": "Temperature is average molecular kinetic energy. Lighter molecules move faster at the same T.", "prereqs": ["ideal-gas", "ke"], "children": [], "order": 26}, "moment-inertia": {"name": "Moment of inertia", "topic": "Rotation", "color": "#9d7bff", "x": 1.6, "y": 0, "level": 0, "leverage": 2, "n_prereq": 0, "latex": "I = \\sum m_i r_i^2 \\;\\; \\text{hoop: } MR^2; \\; \\text{disk: } \\tfrac{1}{2}MR^2; \\; \\text{sphere: } \\tfrac{2}{5}MR^2; \\; \\text{rod (center): } \\tfrac{1}{12}ML^2", "desc": "Rotational mass: resistance to angular acceleration. Mass farther out counts more.", "prereqs": [], "children": ["ang-mom", "rot-ke"], "order": 5}, "momentum": {"name": "Momentum", "topic": "Momentum", "color": "#f2cc8f", "x": -4.800000000000001, "y": -1, "level": 1, "leverage": 4, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "\\mathbf{p} = m \\mathbf{v}", "desc": "Quantity of motion. Conserved in isolated systems, which makes it powerful.", "prereqs": ["newton2"], "children": ["ang-mom", "impulse"], "order": 10}, "momentum-cons": {"name": "Conservation of momentum", "topic": "Momentum", "color": "#f2cc8f", "x": -4.800000000000001, "y": -3, "level": 3, "leverage": 1, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "\\mathbf{p}_{\\text{initial}} = \\mathbf{p}_{\\text{final}} \