nds on length and gravity only, not mass or amplitude.", "prereqs": ["shm"], "children": [], "order": 36}, "power": {"name": "Power", "topic": "Work and Energy", "color": "#81b29a", "x": 1.6, "y": -2, "level": 2, "leverage": 2, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "P = \\frac{dW}{dt} = \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}", "desc": "Rate of energy transfer. A car climbing fast needs more power than one cruising.", "prereqs": ["work-def"], "children": ["intensity"], "order": 24}, "pressure-depth": {"name": "Pressure vs depth", "topic": "Fluids", "color": "#f4845f", "x": -3.2, "y": -2, "level": 2, "leverage": 2, "n_prereq": 2, "latex": "P = P_0 + \\rho g h", "desc": "Pressure grows with depth. Your ears feel it a few meters underwater.", "prereqs": ["density", "weight"], "children": ["bernoulli", "pascal"], "order": 21}, "projectile": {"name": "Projectile motion", "topic": "Kinematics", "color": "#4a6fa5", "x": 6.4, "y": -2, "level": 2, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 1, "latex": "x = v_0 \\cos\\theta \\, t, \\quad y = v_0 \\sin\\theta \\, t - \\tfrac{1}{2} g t^2", "desc": "Horizontal velocity is constant; vertical motion is free fall. Range is maximized at 45 degrees.", "prereqs": ["kinematic"], "children": [], "order": 27}, "resonance": {"name": "Resonance on a string", "topic": "Waves", "color": "#6d9dc5", "x": 0.8, "y": -6, "level": 6, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 2, "latex": "f_n = n \\frac{v}{2L}, \\quad n = 1, 2, 3, \\dots", "desc": "Only wavelengths that fit an integer number of half-waves survive. n = 1 is the fundamental.", "prereqs": ["standing-wave", "wave-speed"], "children": [], "order": 50}, "rot-ke": {"name": "Rotational kinetic energy", "topic": "Rotation", "color": "#9d7bff", "x": 3.2, "y": -3, "level": 3, "leverage": 0, "n_prereq": 3, "latex": "K_{\\text{rot}} = \\tfrac{1}{2} I \\omega^2, \\quad v = \\omega r", "desc": "Rolling without slipping: total K is translational plus rotational.", "prereqs": ["ke", "moment-inertia", "rot-kin"], "children": [], "order": 34}, "rot-kin"